# Session logs written by playing the game — one folder per date, one file per sitting.
#
# These are evidence, not source. They are regenerated every time anybody plays, they are large, and
# two people playing the same afternoon would conflict on files neither of them wrote by hand. What
# is worth keeping out of a session lives in DECISIONS.md or in the notes, not in a transcript.
#
# Scoped to the date folders on purpose. Everything else in this directory is the headless harness's
# committed output — fights.tsv, runs.tsv, levels.md, summary.md and logs/*.log — plus the
# designer's own omarTest/ notes, and all of that stays tracked. A blanket rule here would have
# quietly untracked the lot.
/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]/
